<title>INDIA: India RBI changes interest on expatriate deposits.</title>
<headline>India RBI changes interest on expatriate deposits.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Thursday it has changed the rates of interest on expatriate deposits maintained in foreign currency under the Foreign Currency (Non-Reseident) Accounts (Banks) Scheme.</p>
<p>The revised rates of interest take effect from October 18, 1996.</p>
<p>Period	     Pound     U.S. Dollar   Deutsche    Japanese</p>
<p>		    sterling			 Mark	   yen</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>					(rates in percent per annum)</p>
<p>		     old    new    old new     old new	old new</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>six months</p>
<p>and above but</p>
<p>less than 1 yr  4.75  4.75     4.5  4.5     3.0  3.0   0.75 0.5</p>
<p>1 yr and above</p>
<p>but less than</p>
<p>2 yrs	     6.50  6.25     6.25 6.0     3.75 3.5   1.0 1.0</p>
<p>2 yrs and above</p>
<p>but less than</p>
<p>3 yrs	     7.25  6.75     6.75 6.25    4.5  4.25  1.5 1.25</p>
<p>3 yrs only	7.50  7.00     7.00 6.50    5.0  4.75  2.0 1.75</p>
